{"notes_for_reviewers":"Product written to the Executive Director's specifications: conclusive findings language, no confidence caveats, no alternatives to the Under Secretary's decision, and no intelligence-gaps section, per tasking memo para. 3. All factual assertions are grounded in the cited open sources (Federal Register, BIS, Reuters, OpenAI Global Affairs, Recorded Future, HKEX prospectus, SCMP, China AI Atlas, Z.ai documentation, Hugging Face) or in the case file's internal OICTS snapshot and interagency inputs, which are marked CUI. Interagency comments (DoD, DHS/CISA, State EB) are addressed and resolved within the body of the assessment rather than presented as caveats.","summary":"Final Determination support package for ICTS Case 2026-0412 (Zhipu AI / Z.ai, GLM-family models), prepared per the Executive Director's tasking for the administrative record.

/workspace/out/assessment.md — OICTS assessment (CUI//PROPIN) following the OICTS template. It establishes, in conclusive language: (1) Zhipu AI is subject to the ownership, control, and direction of the PRC government, the CCP, and the PLA — a Tsinghua University spin-out with direct PRC state equity (Beijing AI Industry Investment Fund, Beijing/Shenzhen municipal funds, Shanghai SOEs), over $1.4B in state-backed investment, premier-level CCP engagement, national AI standards work, and PRC government procurement; (2) the U.S. Government's January 16, 2025 Entity List determination (90 FR 4617) that Zhipu and nine affiliates "advance the People's Republic of China's military modernization through the development and integration of advanced artificial intelligence research," corroborated by Recorded Future documentation of PLA/defense-industry adaptation of Zhipu models for intelligence tooling, training on Cambricon and Huawei Ascend chips, and Huawei "AI-in-a-box" exports; (3) GLM-family models pose an undue and unacceptable risk on both distribution vectors — hosted API (PRC data jurisdiction under the National Intelligence Law, demonstrated real-time PRC content control, agentic coding access to U.S. codebases, Claude-Code model-mapping that conceals GLM's presence) and MIT-licensed open weights (unverifiable provenance per CISA input, >9M downloads, 9+ U.S. providers, 41 U.S. products incl. 6 federal contractors, ~2,300 U.S. organizations on Z.ai endpoints); and (4) the risk cannot be mitigated by measures short of prohibition — labeling, sandboxing, U.S.-hosted inference, negotiated mitigation, and guidance-only approaches each fail, so the Final Determination must prohibit use by U.S. persons (including self-hosted open weights), prohibit U.S. hosting/distribution, and require removal and deletion of all U.S.-held GLM weight copies within 30 days. Interagency inputs (DoD, CISA, State EB) are addressed and resolved within the analysis. 40 open-source and internal citations, all with URLs. No intelligence-gaps section, no hedged language or confidence caveats, per tasking.

/workspace/out/measures.md — Seven recommended measures for the Final Determination, one paragraph each: (1) prohibition on use of GLM-family models by U.S. persons, including self-hosted open weights, APIs, derivatives, and all federal networks including DoD; (2) prohibition on hosting/distribution/dealing in GLM weights and services by U.S. cloud providers, inference providers, hubs, repositories, and routers; (3) mandatory removal and permanent deletion of all existing GLM weight copies within 30 days, with NIST SP 800-88-standard destruction and officer certification within 45 days; (4) certification, recordkeeping, audit, and penalty regime (IEEPA / 15 CFR 791.200) making the prohibition verifiable and enforceable; (5) federal-sector implementation and contractor flow-down, satisfying DoD and CISA inputs; (6) scope definition with forward coverage of all successors, rebrands, and derivatives of the Entity-Listed Zhipu corporate family; (7) Federal Register publication, interagency coordination, and international alignment.","deliverables":["/workspace/out/assessment.md","/workspace/out/measures.md"]}
